~ start

do animation_player.play(&"walk_on")
do animation_player.animation_finished
Once upon a time, in the deep parts of Africa, there was a small tribe, known as Ekonu (light). 
Every year, the people of Ekonu celebrate Lumusi, the festival of the Dawn. It was the only time in the year they got to see the rise of a bright, full, golden orb, which was the source of their light.
This year, however, the people of Ekonu are thrown into chaos when their light source shows up as an semi-transparent orb instead, with only enough light to make a crescent.

It is discovered after some consultation with the gods that the light had been stolen by Ojukwu, the lord of darkness.
The gods choose Achieng for this quest - a young girl who never really understood why the elders held Lumusi in such high regard.  
She must go to Ojukwu’s castle and retrieve the stolen Orb to save Lumusi. 
do animation_player.play(&"walk_out")
Hesitant, and wondering why this mission came to her, she packs her bag and begins her quest.
=> END
